checkly:index/check:Check.description:
Checks allows you to monitor key webapp flows, backend API's and set up alerting, so you get a notification when things break or slow down.

The <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.Check`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.Check`" pulumi-lang-go="`Check`" pulumi-lang-python="`Check`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.Check`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.Check`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_check`">`checkly.Check`</span> resource type is deprecated in favor of <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_api_check`">`checkly.ApiCheck`</span>, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_browser_check`">`checkly.BrowserCheck`</span> and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_multistep_check`">`checkly.MultistepCheck`</span>, which only expose the attributes of their check type, and will be removed in a future version of the provider. An existing check can be moved to its per-type resource with a Pulumi alias, without recreating it. Before moving a check, see "Moving to the replacement resources" in [Upgrading to v3](https://github.com/checkly/pulumi-checkly#upgrading-to-v3) for what to change: <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_api_check`">`checkly.ApiCheck`</span> has lower default <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`degradedResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DegradedResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-go="`degradedResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-python="`degraded_response_time`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`degradedResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-java="`degradedResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`degraded_response_time`">`degradedResponseTime`</span> and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`maxResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`MaxResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-go="`maxResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-python="`max_response_time`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`maxResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-java="`maxResponseTime`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`max_response_time`">`maxResponseTime`</span> values and follows redirects by default, and the per-type resources have no <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DoubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`double_check`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`double_check`">`doubleCheck`</span>.

## Example Usage

