## Moving to the per-type resources

An existing check can be moved to the resource of its type, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.ApiCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_api_check`">`checkly.ApiCheck`</span>, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.BrowserCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_browser_check`">`checkly.BrowserCheck`</span> or <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.MultistepCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_multistep_check`">`checkly.MultistepCheck`</span>, without recreating it: declare the new resource with an alias to the old type, `checkly:index/check:Check`, and run `pulumi up`. Refresh the stack on v3 before you add the alias. The provider can't verify the check type during the move, so pick the resource that matches the check's <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`type`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Type`" pulumi-lang-go="`type`" pulumi-lang-python="`type`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`type`" pulumi-lang-java="`type`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`type`">`type`</span>. The per-type resources have no <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DoubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-go="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-python="`double_check`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-java="`doubleCheck`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`double_check`">`doubleCheck`</span>, so replace it with the equivalent <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`retryStrategy`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`RetryStrategy`" pulumi-lang-go="`retryStrategy`" pulumi-lang-python="`retry_strategy`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`retryStrategy`" pulumi-lang-java="`retryStrategy`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`retry_strategy`">`retryStrategy`</span> first. For a browser or multi-step check whose <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ShouldFail`" pulumi-lang-go="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-python="`should_fail`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-java="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`should_fail`">`shouldFail`</span> is <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`true`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`True`" pulumi-lang-go="`true`" pulumi-lang-python="`true`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`true`" pulumi-lang-java="`true`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`true`">`true`</span>, remove <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ShouldFail`" pulumi-lang-go="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-python="`should_fail`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-java="`shouldFail`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`should_fail`">`shouldFail`</span> and run `pulumi up` before the move, which sets it to <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`false`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`False`" pulumi-lang-go="`false`" pulumi-lang-python="`false`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`false`" pulumi-lang-java="`false`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`false`">`false`</span>. See "Moving to the replacement resources" in [Upgrading to v3](https://github.com/checkly/pulumi-checkly#upgrading-to-v3) for the details.

