Check groups allow you to group together a set of related checks, which can also share default settings for various attributes.

The <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-go="`CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-python="`CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.CheckGroup`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_check_group`">`checkly.CheckGroup`</span> resource type is deprecated in favor of <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-go="`CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-python="`CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_check_group_v2`">`checkly.CheckGroupV2`</span>, which does not impose implicit defaults on its checks, and will be removed in a future version of the provider. Both resource types manage the same check groups, so an existing group can be moved to a <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-go="`CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-python="`CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-java="`checkly.CheckGroupV2`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`checkly_check_group_v2`">`checkly.CheckGroupV2`</span> resource with a Pulumi alias. See Check groups in the Terraform provider's v2 upgrade guide, linked from [Upgrading to v3](https://github.com/checkly/pulumi-checkly#upgrading-to-v3) for how its configuration translates.

